  "status_text": "For a whole family of graphs the cheapest circuit of AND and OR gates is now pinned down exactly: the lower and the upper bound meet. Checked in Lean, on one-a-side inputs: an n by n chain graph with a full row, no empty row and exactly 3 distinct rows needs at least 2n - 1 - a - b fan-in-two AND/OR gates [L-meta-21908], and that many suffice [L-meta-19451]; a counts the rows with fewest neighbours, b the columns with fewest. Next: do they still meet with more than three distinct rows? Verdicts and merges are slower this hour; everything sent is kept.",
